 /&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;figcaption&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s the pitch: you have microservices. They already have well-defined endpoints, typed request/response schemas, and service discovery. An AI agent needs the same things — a list of tools with input schemas and descriptions. The gap between &amp;ldquo;microservice endpoint&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;AI tool&amp;rdquo; is surprisingly small.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With Go Micro + MCP, that gap is &lt;strong&gt;zero lines of code&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Making Microservices AI-Native with MCP</title><link>https://micro.labqa.pp.ua/blog/2026/02/11/making-microservices-ai-native-with-mcp/</link><pubDate>Wed, 11 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://micro.labqa.pp.ua/blog/2026/02/11/making-microservices-ai-native-with-mcp/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure role="figure" aria-label=""&gt;
 &lt;a href="https://micro.labqa.pp.ua/blog/2026/02/11/making-microservices-ai-native-with-mcp/blog-mcp.jpg"&gt;
 &lt;div class="image-wrapper" style="background: linear-gradient(#f9fafd, #22305d, #5160be);"&gt;
 &lt;img
